    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so you think the focus should be more on how the money is used rather than just the total amount? \n\nbut if we follow that logic, wouldn't there be a limit? like, if a government just keeps printing money or borrowing indefinitely to fund social programs, doesn't that eventually devalue the currency or put an unbearable debt burden on future generations? isn't there a point where the \"distribution\" argument becomes irrelevant because the whole system becomes unstable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
